    description: "From WI-borib (docs/audits/0026). Verdict SINGLE-SOURCE. Agent C's inventory (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/borib_consumer_agreement_10302026/C_counts_disclosure.md, C_scripts/diff_counts.py), real numbers read from the default surveys in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/borib_consumer_agreement_10302026/surveys/.\n\nFACT: how many files of language L. profile.languages counts LANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS globs; each analyzer walks its own finder. They differ for .pyi, *.kts, *.rake, scss/less/sass counted as css (mitmproxy css 62 in the profile, 30 analysed), .lhs/.mli/.sc/.tfvars/.gvy and generic YAML; logrus go 47 vs 46 (a file with no symbols). The profile is computed before --max-file-bytes, so capped files are counted and not analysed; --max-files refusals are recorded nowhere.\nAlso: the sketch Overview's \"N files (A non-test + B test)\" takes B from a separate walk over files with a node, never profile.test_files (which has no reader): mitmproxy 392 vs 355, knex 294 vs 289 (offline reproduction of the sketch logic, not a sketch run). knex has 12,895 nodes and 12,892 distinct ids: three file anchors emitted twice (the analyzer's and orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis'), counted twice by metrics.total_nodes, unflagged by the validator. The profile has no key for analysed pony, scss and gitignore. bakeoff-broad / bakeoff-deep each carry a private 18-extension detect_languages.\n\nACCEPTANCE: the profile's per-language file set and the analyzers' candidate sets come from one table (or the difference is a named field); node ids unique per map, enforced."  # d69f
